  2→//! Tensor Vault: Secure secret storage with graph-based access control.
  3→//!
  4→//! Secrets are encrypted at rest using AES-256-GCM. Access is controlled
  5→//! by graph topology - a requester must have a path to the secret node.
  6→//!
  7→//! Security features:
  8→//! - AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption
  9→//! - Argon2id key derivation (GPU/ASIC resistant)
 10→//! - Key obfuscation via HMAC (hides secret names in storage)
 11→//! - Metadata encryption (hides creator, timestamps)
 12→//! - Length padding (hides plaintext size)
 13→//! - Pointer indirection (hides storage patterns)
 14→//! - Graph-based access control (topological authorization)
